From: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: net: dsa: qca8k: fix the MDIO bulk read offset

qca8k_bulk_read() falls back to reading the registers one by one over
MDIO when no management conduit is available. It stores register i at
val_buf + i, and val_buf is a void pointer, so the words land one byte
apart and overwrite each other. Every multi-register read is then
garbage: the ARL table read used by the FDB dump, the FDB search and
the MDB insert/delete.

With the QCA header the reads mostly go over Ethernet, so the fallback
is rarely taken. With tag_8021q there is no management conduit and
every bulk read takes it.

Index the buffer as an array of u32.
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -516,7 +516,7 @@ qca8k_bulk_read(void *ctx, const void *r
 
 	/* loop count times and increment reg of 4 */
 	for (i = 0; i < count; i++, reg += sizeof(u32)) {
-		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, val_buf + i);
+		ret = qca8k_read_mii(priv, reg, (u32 *)val_buf + i);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 	}
